    {
      "id": "5b095b09-0000-4000-8000-000000000041",
      "name": "Sample orders",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        440,
        900
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Sample orders, shaped like WooCommerce's. Replace this node with your shop's \"Get order\" node.\nconst day = (n) => DateTime.now().minus({ days: n }).toISO();\nconst orders = [\n  { number: '1001', status: 'completed', date_created: day(12), date_completed: day(8), total: '68.00', currency: 'EUR',\n    billing: { email: 'ada@example.com' },\n    line_items: [{ name: 'Linen shirt', quantity: 1, total: '49.00' }, { name: 'Canvas tote bag', quantity: 1, total: '19.00' }] },\n  { number: '1002', status: 'processing', date_created: day(1), date_completed: null, total: '120.00', currency: 'EUR',\n    billing: { email: 'bob@example.com' },\n    line_items: [{ name: 'Wool coat', quantity: 1, total: '120.00' }] },\n  { number: '1003', status: 'completed', date_created: day(70), date_completed: day(65), total: '35.00', currency: 'EUR',\n    billing: { email: 'carla@example.com' },\n    line_items: [{ name: 'Leather belt', quantity: 1, total: '35.00' }] },\n  { number: '1004', status: 'cancelled', date_created: day(20), date_completed: null, total: '15.00', currency: 'EUR',\n    billing: { email: 'dan@example.com' },\n    line_items: [{ name: 'Cotton socks (3 pairs)', quantity: 1, total: '15.00' }] },\n  { number: '1005', status: 'completed', date_created: day(6), date_completed: day(3), total: '42.00', currency: 'EUR',\n    billing: { email: 'elise@example.fr' },\n    line_items: [{ name: 'Ceramic mug set', quantity: 1, total: '42.00' }] },\n];\nreturn orders.map((o) => ({ json: o }));"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "5b095b09-0000-4000-8000-000000000042",
      "name": "Matching order",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        660,
        900
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const want = $('When called by the agent').first().json;\nconst number = String(want.orderNumber ?? '').replace(/[^0-9A-Za-z-]/g, '');\nconst email = String(want.email ?? '').trim().toLowerCase();\nconst order = $input.all().map((i) => i.json).find((o) => String(o.number ?? o.id) === number);\nif (!number || !email || !order || String(order.billing?.email ?? '').toLowerCase() !== email) {\n  return [{ json: { found: false, message: 'No order matches this number and email address.' } }];\n}\nconst days = $('Return policy').first().json.returnDays;\nconst statusText = { pending: 'waiting for payment', processing: 'being prepared, not shipped yet', 'on-hold': 'on hold',\n  completed: 'shipped', cancelled: 'cancelled', refunded: 'refunded', failed: 'payment failed' }[order.status] ?? order.status;\nconst shipped = order.date_completed ? DateTime.fromISO(order.date_completed) : null;\nconst returnUntil = shipped ? shipped.plus({ days }) : null;\nconst returnable = order.status === 'completed' && returnUntil !== null && returnUntil >= DateTime.now();\nreturn [{ json: {\n  found: true,\n  number: String(order.number ?? order.id),\n  status: statusText,\n  placedOn: DateTime.fromISO(order.date_created).toFormat('d LLLL yyyy'),\n  shippedOn: shipped ? shipped.toFormat('d LLLL yyyy') : null,\n  items: order.line_items.map((l) => l.quantity + ' × ' + l.name).join(', '),\n  total: order.total + ' ' + order.currency,\n  returnable,\n  returnNote: returnable ? 'Can be returned until ' + returnUntil.toFormat('d LLLL yyyy') + '.'\n    : order.status === 'completed' ? 'The ' + days + '-day return window has passed.' : 'Only a shipped order can be returned.',\n  // This shop's \"completed\" is a parcel sent: say shipped, which WooCommerce's word alone does not.\n  card: { number: String(order.number ?? order.id), status: order.status === 'completed' ? 'shipped' : order.status, date_created: order.date_created,\n    line_items: order.line_items, total: order.total, currency: order.currency },\n} }];"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "5b095b09-0000-4000-8000-000000000043",
      "name": "Note 43",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -680,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Order status and returns in your shop's website chat\n\nA visitor asks in the chat on your shop where their order is, or wants to return something. The agent looks the order up by **number and email**, tells its status, and for a return asks which items and why, with a photo if the item is damaged. The visitor **confirms with a button**, the return is saved in a data table, and your support team gets an email.\n\n### Requirements\n- An n8n instance the visitor's browser can reach on a public URL, with data tables. Tested on n8n 2.45.7.\n- An OpenAI API key, or credentials for any other chat model n8n supports that can call tools.\n- An SMTP account to email your support team, or swap **Tell support** for Gmail, Outlook or Slack.\n\n### Set up\n1. Open **Settings**: your shop's name, the support address, the sender address. `richCards` adds a card under the answer (the order, the booking) as a code block: the aparté chat widget for n8n draws it, n8n's own chat shows it as code. Turn it off for n8n's chat.\n2. Add your credentials to **Chat model** and **Tell support**.\n3. Connect your orders (see the note under the workflow), and set the return window in **Return policy**.\n4. Open **When chat message received**, put your site in **Allowed Origins**, then **publish** the workflow and copy the production URL that ends in `/chat`.\n5. Paste this in your page, with your URL:\n\n```html\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@aparte/n8n-chat@0.3.0/dist/style.css\">\n<script type=\"module\">\n  import { createChat } from 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@aparte/n8n-chat@0.3.0/dist/cdn/n8n-chat.js';\n  createChat({ webhookUrl: 'YOUR_PRODUCTION_URL', allowFileUploads: true });\n</script>\n```\n\nThat widget is [@aparte/n8n-chat](https://github.com/apartejs/n8n-chat) (MIT): it shows the confirm buttons inside the conversation, lets the visitor drop or paste a photo, and keeps the conversation after a reload. n8n's own widget (`@n8n/chat`) works with this workflow too.",
        "width": 620,
        "height": 1160,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "5b095b09-0000-4000-8000-000000000044",
      "name": "Note 44",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2380,
        -160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### The visitor confirms\nThe agent only *requests* a return. The workflow looks the order up again, checks it can be returned and has no open return, then shows **Open the return** / **Keep my order**. The photo attached to the message that asked for the return goes to support with the email; if the email fails, the return is still saved.\n\nThe agent answers in the visitor's language; the button labels and the replies after them are written in **Confirm with buttons**, **Return opened** and **Order kept**: translate them for your site.",
        "width": 760,
        "height": 200,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "5b095b09-0000-4000-8000-000000000045",
      "name": "Note 45",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        760
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Connect your orders\n**Sample orders** holds five test orders in WooCommerce's shape (try order 1001 with ada@example.com). Replace it with your shop's node: a WooCommerce **Order → Get** with the order ID `{{ $json.orderNumber }}`, or a Shopify or HTTP Request node mapped to the same fields (`number`, `status`, `billing.email`, `line_items`, `date_created`, `date_completed`, `total`, `currency`).\n\n**Matching order** only answers when the number and the email both match, and gives the same answer when they do not, so the chat never reveals that an order exists.",
        "width": 900,
        "height": 300,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "5b095b09-0000-4000-8000-000000000046",
      "name": "Note 46",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1040,
        720
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Memory and limits\n**Simple Memory** lives in n8n's process: it is lost on a restart and does not work in queue mode. In production, use Postgres or Redis Chat Memory with the same settings.\n\nThe chat model must be able to call tools. The return is a request: refunds, labels and stock stay with your team.",
        "width": 620,
        "height": 240,
        "color": 7
      }
    }
  ],
